   "transcript_text": "person_2 (DOCTOR) 336.61-339.75s: What are the chances it's something bad?",
   "start_timestamp": "00:00:00.61",
   "end_timestamp": "00:00:00.75",
   "supports": []
  },
  {
   "evidence_id": "EV_001",
   "speaker_id": "person_2",
   "speaker_role": "doctor",
   "transcript_text": "person_2 (DOCTOR) 340.56-361.46s: I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's insomnia, probably stress-related, and we'll know more once the a sleep study is back. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had trouble sleeping for two months, severe, and no snoring or low mood.",
   "start_timestamp": "00:00:00.56",
   "end_timestamp": "00:00:00.46",
   "supports": []
  },
  {
   "evidence_id": "EV_001",
   "speaker_id": "person_2",
   "speaker_role": "doctor",
   "transcript_text": "person_2 (DOCTOR) 364.50-394.70s: Let's get a sleep study, for insomnia. Let's book a thyroid test to look into insomnia. Same wake-up time every day, no screens in the hour before bed, and no coffee after lunch. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. I'd like you back in four weeks. Okay, we're done for today. Take care.",
